  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "omega-kotlin publishes the whole modifier run of a declaration as one definition.modifier_candidate name, not one fact per annotation, so a composable is recognised by the @Composable-first and @Preview-first spellings only; `@Inject @Composable fun` is not reached.",
      "A destination's content is a trailing lambda and a call fact spans only the callee identifier, so `composable(\"home\") { HomeScreen() }` states the route and the graph that declares it, never that the route renders HomeScreen. The screen is reached instead by the renders edge from the NavHost composable.",
      "A route written as a string literal and a route written as a constant reference are different identities: `composable(\"home\")` and `navigate(\"home\")` meet, `composable(Screen.Home.route)` and `navigate(Screen.Home.route)` meet, the two spellings mixed do not. `navigation(startDestination = ..., route = ...)` names both its arguments, so its own route is not read.",
      "A concrete navigate argument does not meet a parameterized declaration: `navigate(\"details/1\")` normalizes to /details/1 and `composable(\"details/{id}\")` to /details/{}.",
      "Composable calls are resolved by simple name across the repository because Kotlin import resolution is not part of an overlay fact; two composables of the same name are one node.",
      "compiler-plugin lowering, slot table, recomposition and the runtime UI tree are outside static source truth."
    ]
  },
